  "body": "## What this changes\n\nThe desktop shell had no logo. `app-icon.png` was a 2,567-byte \"MC\" monogram committed as a real file, while `desktop_assets.py` described it as a runtime placeholder for an asset that \"has not shipped\" — so nothing rendered the product's actual mark, and there was no way to put it in a Start Menu entry or a Dock.\n\nThis ships the owner's designed mark and an opt-in `--desktop` / `-Desktop` installer flag that creates a native launcher per platform.\n\n## The mark\n\nKeyed to transparency with an **un-blend**, not a colour threshold:\n\n```\nC = (observed - (1-a)*bg) / a\n```\n\nThe source background is a flat `#050c1d`, and a plain threshold leaves a navy fringe on every antialiased edge — which is precisely what shows up at 16px.\n\n**Two PNG renders ship on purpose**, not one file scaled at render time. A tray draws at 16–24px, where the 10% margin the app icon wants shrinks the glyph below legibility, so `tray-icon.png` is the same mark cut at 2%.\n\n| Asset | Margin | Size | Use |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `app-icon.png` | 10% | 256², RGBA | window / taskbar / docs |\n| `app-icon.ico` | 10% | 16–256 multi-size | Windows `.lnk` |\n| `app-icon.icns` | 10% | 16–512 slots | macOS `.app` |\n| `tray-icon.png` | **2%** | 128², RGBA | tray at 16–24px |\n\nPalette quantising was tried and reverted: it folds the fully transparent background into a nearest palette entry with non-zero alpha, shipping a faint box behind the mark. Caught by probing the decoded alpha channel for a zero value and not finding one.\n\n## A shipped bug caught before merge\n\n`mcc-desktop` is a `[project.gui-scripts]` entry, so `mcc-desktop.exe` is a **GUI-subsystem** binary and PowerShell's call operator does not wait for it. The first version exported the icon through `Invoke-NativeCommand`, then pointed `IconLocation` at the result:\n\n```\ncall-operator returned after : 476 ms\nLASTEXITCODE                 : 0          <- false success\nicon exists IMMEDIATELY after: False      <- shortcut points at nothing\nicon exists after 6s         : True\n```\n\nA shortcut with a blank icon, reported as success. Now uses `Start-Process -Wait -PassThru` and verifies the file exists before use. Same class as the earlier `$argumentsLiteral` and `.Count` installer failures: parse-clean, runtime-broken, reports success.\n\n## Verification\n\n**The assets are in the wheel** — listed, not inferred from the packaging config:\n\n```\nmy_claude_code/assets/app-icon.icns   356091\nmy_claude_code/assets/app-icon.ico    115462\nmy_claude_code/assets/app-icon.png     72585\nmy_claude_code/assets/tray-icon.png    28535\n```\n\nHatch picks them up automatically because they sit under the package, so no force-include was needed.\n\n- Wheel installed into an isolated `UV_TOOL_DIR`; `mcc-desktop --export-icon` produced byte-exact `.ico`/`.icns`/`.png`.\n- `install.sh` parses under `sh -n` (LF-normalised, per the CRLF trap); `install.ps1` parses via the PowerShell AST parser with zero errors. `New-DesktopShortcut` is defined and called 3×, matching `Enable-RtkForAgents`.\n- Brand hex **sampled from the shipped asset**, not invented: darkest `#9f1131`, lightest `#dd2643`, average `#b22242` — all near Velvet's `#e6435e`, so no new accent token.\n- `tests/contracts/` 176 passed — README anchors and the provider table intact.\n\n**Full suite: 6 failed, 4231 passed, 26 skipped.** Baseline on unmodified `fork/main`, measured in the same shell with `ENABLE_WEB_SERVER_TOOLS`/`EXA_API_KEY` neutralised: **6 failed, 4214 passed**. Same six PowerShell installer failures, +17 new tests, zero new failures.\n\nruff format, ruff check, ty: clean.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- The macOS `.app` bundle and Linux `.desktop` entry are written to spec and syntax-checked but **were not run on real macOS or Linux** — this is a Windows machine. The Windows shortcut path was exercised end to end.\n- The tray still reads `app_icon_bytes(\".png\")` rather than the new `tray_icon_bytes()`, so it gets the 10% render. `desktop_tray.py` is owned by the window PR in flight and the one-line wiring lands there — deliberately not touched here to avoid a collision.\n- `--desktop` is opt-in; a default install is byte-identical to before apart from the replaced asset.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
